Z||000000||batboy||03-04-2001||01:44 PM||||I love upgrading and tweaking on my home computer. OMG, I'm becoming a geek! I switched out my Celeron 566 that I was normally running at 952 MHz, although it would benchmark and play games at 978, but not 100% stable (it would also post at 1020, but crash in Windows).<P>Added a P-3 cC0 stepping 700 chip. I'm now cruising at 1.05 gig @ 1.9v rock steady. See the below pic for benchmarks at 1071 MHz, which is max speed on my motherboad for that chip. I also have to use 1.95v at that speed which is also max. Not 100% stable, but after the CPU "burns in" (like seating piston rings on a new engine) and with some more cooling tweaks. I hope to be there.<P>But for now, 1050 MHz rocks! I'm dancin' the 1 gig jig! Because this P-III 700 FC-PGA has twice the L2 cache as my ol' Celly, this baby is posting incredible benchmarks compared to what I was getting before. Look at the graph, one of my Sandra CPU benchmark scores beat out a P-4... hahaha... for 3 times cheaper too... hahaha... take that Intel!<P>Here is my system: P-III cC0 700/1050 MHz @ 1.9v (totally stable), lapped GlobalWin FOP38 cooler, Arctic Silver Ultra, Abit SE6, 256 meg of PC-133 Infineon RAM, Antec 300w PS, rounded data cables, lots of extra fans & cooling mods to case, mobo, & GeForce II MX AGP video card, Sound Blaster Live X-Gamer 5.1, US Robotics 56k modem, Kenwood True-X CD-ROM, HP CD-Writer, 13 and 40 gig Maxtor harddrives, etc...<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1071-P3.jpg"> ||||reg||6
